WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.488 --> 00:00:11.040
In most cities today, a fair price for wedding-parent makeup runs from about 200,000 to 300,000 won.

2
00:00:11.376 --> 00:00:17.976
Prices vary depending on who's doing it and where you are.

3
00:00:18.312 --> 00:00:31.128
What you're paying for is a specialist personally handling you, a one-on-one consultation, and at least 90 minutes of dedicated, undivided service.

4
00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:39.192
It covers more than just makeup application — it includes advanced correcting techniques and the cost of premium products.

5
00:00:39.528 --> 00:00:45.720
Some places charge a premium under a "head artist rate," but that's not the norm,

6
00:00:46.056 --> 00:00:55.896
and while some planner packages run just over 100,000 won, those usually put a junior part-timer on you or tack on extra fees (lashes,

7
00:00:56.232 --> 00:01:01.776
hair fiber powder, and so on) — so check the details carefully.
